  "summary": "I graduated from Union College with a Bachelor’s of Science degree in Computer Engineering with a minor in Latin American and Caribbean Studies. After being introduced to Python in a robotics course, my interest shifted from Electrical Engineering to Computer Engineering. What I find most enjoyable about technology is how it is constantly changing and growing. It improves human lives by allowing us to solve problems through simulating a solution or using the internet as a source of information. Through the induction process for my fraternity, I experienced personal growth in leadership and became more open minded. It has encouraged and allowed me to step out of my comfort zone and expand my horizons.\n\nOne proud accomplishment was being able to successfully implement the game of Set in Java while working in a group of four. We grasped the concept of UML diagrams and created the corresponding use case, activity, and sequence diagrams. The work was divided evenly amongst us where we each implemented two classes. The project improved my debugging and communication skills. In the future, I plan to become a Full Stack Developer where I can contribute to both front and back-end services.",
